 the partnership  worth 40 million euros a year had  previously already attracted criticism  russia is being told clearly that at  present it is unwelcome in the world of  sports  one of the first athletes to openly  condemn vladimir putin's aggression in  ukraine was vladislav  just weeks ago you may have seen his  face and his call for peace during the  winter olympics in beijing he's the  ukrainian skeleton athlete who put his  no war message out there after one of  his runs at the games as russia was  amassing nearly 200 000 troops on his  country's borders  vladislavian joins me now from northwest  ukraine welcome to dw  uh the ioc and china both said that  athletes shouldn't protest but you did  so anyway tell us about that moment  i i would not call it protest it's  i will call it call  because i'm not mention any other  country i just mentioned my country and  that i want to peace in my country and i  want a peace for people who lives in my  country  and i mean you're back home now and  you're in and out of bomb shelters and  you could even be asked to fight have  you heard anything yet and  do explain for our viewers what the  situation is like where you are  now where you are where i am it's now  for a moment uh  only syrians play but i don't hear  explosions but i hear it that morning at  yesterday evening so  it's absolutely terrible to see what i  see and  i spoke with my friends  around the ukraine and  it's it's terrible situation they like  russian attacks  kids they attack civilians  so it's it's terrible and  it's terrible that our all families in  ukraine's suffering now  because of this invasion and  it's i hope it will end shortly  that's understandable have you um been  spoken to about joining forces to help  fight has that been a discussion you've  had yet  i wonder but  suddenly i don't have any experience in  military sync i'm not a professional  soldier i'm a  professional artist an olympian so i  fight on a my platform and i  fight on  my 